<title>JAPAN: Saudi Aramco cuts May propane to $179/T -- traders.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco cuts May propane to $179/T -- traders.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia's state-owned oil firm Saudi Aramco has cut its propane contract price for May by $19 from the previous month to $179 per tonne and its price for butane by $15 to $192 per tonne, traders said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The propane price for May is up $4 from a year ago, and that for butane up $12 over the same period.</p>
<p>The Saudi contract price is loosely based on the results of three monthly spot tenders and the company's own assessment of spot market trends.</p>
</text>
